    {
      "id": "table-4",
      "line": 372,
      "heading_context": "## Decision Cheat Sheet",
      "headers": [
        "Decision",
        "Use When",
        "Avoid When / Watch Out For"
      ],
      "rows": [
        [
          "**Stack allocation** (`int x;`, `int a[N];`)",
          "Size known at compile time; lifetime is function-scoped; N is small (< a few KB)",
          "Large arrays (stack overflow); lifetime must outlive current scope"
        ],
        [
          "**Heap allocation** (`malloc`)",
          "Size determined at runtime; lifetime must outlive function; large buffers",
          "Forgetting `free` (leak); double-free (UB); always check for NULL return"
        ],
        [
          "**`malloc(n)`**",
          "Allocating uninitialized memory you will fully write before reading",
          "Uninitialized reads are UB — use `calloc` if you need zero-init"
        ],
        [
          "**`calloc(count, size)`**",
          "Zero-initialized array of count elements; integer overflow protection in size calc",
          "Slower than malloc due to zeroing; still must `free`"
        ],
        [
          "**`realloc(ptr, newsize)`**",
          "Growing/shrinking an existing heap block",
          "May return a different pointer — always assign return value; passing a freed pointer = UB"
        ],
        [
          "**`free(ptr)`**",
          "Every `malloc`/`calloc`/`realloc` must have exactly one `free`",
          "Double-free = UB; `free(NULL)` is safe (no-op)"
        ],
        [
          "**Pointer** (`int *p`)",
          "Nullable (can be NULL); pointer arithmetic needed; passing large structs by reference",
          "Array decay: `int a[]` passed to function becomes `int *` — size lost"
        ],
        [
          "**Array** (`int a[N]`)",
          "Fixed-size, stack-allocated collection; sizeof gives full size within declaring scope",
          "Decays to pointer when passed to function — pass size separately"
        ],
        [
          "**`static` storage class**",
          "Variable that persists across function calls (local static); file-scope variable hidden from other TUs",
          "Local statics are not thread-safe (C11 `_Thread_local` for thread-local)"
        ],
        [
          "**`extern` storage class**",
          "Declare a symbol defined in another translation unit",
          "Not a definition — no storage allocated; must match type exactly"
        ],
        [
          "**`auto` storage class**",
          "Default for local variables; rarely written explicitly",
          "Redundant keyword in C (every local is auto by default)"
        ],
        [
          "**`signed` integers**",
          "Arithmetic where negative values are meaningful",
          "Overflow is **undefined behavior** — compiler may delete \"impossible\" checks"
        ],
        [
          "**`unsigned` integers**",
          "Bit manipulation, sizes, indices, modular arithmetic",
          "Underflow wraps silently: `0u - 1` = `UINT_MAX`; mixing signed/unsigned in comparisons promotes to unsigned"
        ],
        [
          "**C99 features** (`//` comments, `for` init, designated initializers, VLAs, `<stdint.h>`)",
          "Default baseline for new code",
          "VLAs are optional in C11+; avoid them"
        ],
        [
          "**C11 features** (`_Atomic`, `_Generic`, `_Static_assert`, threads)",
          "Portable atomics, type-generic macros, compile-time assertions",
          "VLAs made optional; `<threads.h>` not universally implemented"
        ],
        [
          "**C23 features** (`nullptr`, `bool`/`true`/`false` as keywords, `#embed`, `typeof`)",
          "Modern compilers targeting latest standard",
          "Compiler support varies; check target toolchain before adopting"
        ]
      ]
    },
